Subject: gnu tar 1.11.8 on DUNIX 4.0 -- won't compile -- fnmatch() problem
Date: 1996/09/09
Message-ID: <FINEMAN.96Sep8210447@grizzly.cs.washington.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 179382969
x-nntp-posting-host: grizzly.cs.washington.edu
sender: news@beaver.cs.washington.edu (USENET News System)
organization: Computer Science & Engineering, U of Washington, Seattle
newsgroups: comp.unix.osf.misc,comp.unix.osf.osf1



Hey all!    

I'm trying to compile gnu tar 1.11.8 on a Dec Alpha running DUNIX 4.0
(a.k.a. osf4.0).  Unfortunately, it just ain't happening.

After doing a configure, the compilation tells me this:

-----------------
gcc -c -DHAVE_CONFIG_H -I.. -I../intl -I. -I../lib  -g -O tar.c
tar.c: In function `name_match':
tar.c:477: `FNM_LEADING_DIR' undeclared (first use this function)
tar.c:477: (Each undeclared identifier is reported only once
tar.c:477: for each function it appears in.)
tar.c: In function `name_scan':
tar.c:608: `FNM_LEADING_DIR' undeclared (first use this function)
tar.c: In function `check_exclude':
tar.c:828: `FNM_LEADING_DIR' undeclared (first use this function)
*** Exit 1
-----------------

Anyways, I noted that on a linux system of mine,
/usr/include/fnmatch.h has this line:

---------
#define	FNM_LEADING_DIR	(1 << 3) /* Ignore `/...' after a match.  */
---------

However, /usr/include/fnmatch.h on the DUNIX system has no such line!

There are several calls to the library function fnmatch() in tar.c
that are sent the parameter FNM_LEADING_DIR, which makes no sense to
the DUNIX libraries.  Man pages on the Linux system do not mention
what the FNM_LEADING_DIR should do / does...

Thoughts?

Thanks, and please mail me with any replies,
Dan Fineman
fineman@cs.washington.edu



