Satish Balay wrote:
 
>         I need to pass the ld flag -rpath from cc, and I tried:
>         cc -rpath PATH -o outputfile [ other_cc_stuff]
...
>         Is there an option equivalent to gcc's -Wl for cc?

-Wl, will work.  The cc(1) manpage describes which -Wx, options map
to which phases of the compilation.

For example, the following cc line will pass the -v verbose flag
to the linker.
	cc a.c -Wl,-v

Joe



