Hi,
I'm setting up a DEC alpha running OSF version 3.2G and am having problems
setting up a non-DEC postscript printer (an Apple Laserwriter Select 360
to be exact).

I have looked through appropriate dxbook books but always come to the
advice of looking for the required information from the printer
manufacturer. 

I am trying to run the printer through the parallel port. When setting it
up using the lprsetup util, it demands to know what type of printer I am
using. I followed someones suggestion of setting it to be an ln03r but
that just resulted in endless 'waiting for device to come online'
messages. I then set the printer type to unknown and was able to print
postscript files (such as those generated by dvips) acceptably but of
course printing straight text files wouldn't work. I then tried to set the
ps parameter in printcap to be LPS. Now I can get some limited output of
straight text files but the beginning of each line is moved further and
further from the right side of the page. Has anybody set this type of
printer (or just a generic non DEC postscript printer) up successfully and
could give me some advice. In case it has any impact upon anybody's
suggestions, I have been out of the unix world for about 3 years; in fact,
the last unix machine that I "managed" as a grad student was a sun 4/110
running sunos 4.1.1!

Thanks in advance for any answers/suggestions.
Sincerely,
Bruce F. Antolovich



